/-!
# Declaration-based Prime candidate integration

This umbrella assembles source admission, wire operations, operational services
and checked language consumers for one declaration-based candidate. Its reusable
mathematical dependencies are owned by `TypeTheory.Calculi.ParameterizedPiSigmaId`,
`TypeTheory.Calculi.CumulativePiSigmaId`, `Logic`, `GSLT` and `Machines`; they do not
depend on this assembly. Dialect comparison policies remain separate experiments.
Importing the assembly neither selects Prime's final syntax nor identifies a
runtime with its mathematical interpretation.

The development exposes:

* an exact decidable algebra of universe levels;
* disjoint sealed-Legacy and cumulative-Tower presentations;
* the exact sealed conservativity frontier and its raw-syntax counterexample;
* structural and typed substitution, including context-comprehension laws;
* a separately named formation-sensitive candidate on the cumulative syntax,
  with retained declaration, binder, pair and conversion-target formation;
  renaming, simultaneous substitution and regularity in formed contexts;
  a real polymorphic identity and a dangling-declaration rejection; and a
  formed-endpoint conversion counterexample showing that these structural
  guarantees alone do not qualify arbitrary conversion or imply normalization;
  root beta preservation under an explicit Pi-conversion boundary, proved
  for the full Tower conversion with opaque constants by complete development;
  formation-sensitive admission of every existing primitive/chain hypothesis
  program and every finite native list-relator spine, retaining independent
  relational denotation and exact proof-relevant list evidence;
  the existing intrinsic atom/arrow fragment and its substitutions translate
  to the same refined judgments, with conversion exact on the translated
  image but no recovery of erased internal type annotations;
* generic dependent beta subject reduction derived from typed simultaneous
  substitution, together with a representation boundary showing that the
  binder-exposing LF encoding commutes with generic binder instantiation while
  canonical declaration-aware tower data does not; both encodings remain
  lossless and conserve exact distinctions, so a checked adapter must preserve
  operational binder structure in addition to syntax; the exact zero-trace
  decode--substitute--reencode adapter reflects every successful result to
  intrinsic substitution, preserves typing, and rejects malformed bodies,
  while remaining explicitly short of an authored inference presentation;
* calibrated four-face beta experiments connecting native typing, authored
  GSLT checking, independent function semantics, and set-valued graphs: the
  dependent cell retains a formed `B, g, a` telescope and requires separate
  exact certificates for the contractum `g a` and its opened type `B a`;
* one declaration-aware typing spine, with proof-carrying signatures,
  monotone extension, exact empty-signature recovery, and a proved
  correspondence to the former declaration calculus;
* the category of declaration-aware well-formed contexts and typed
  substitutions, with constructive terminal empty context, type and term
  reindexing, and the full context-comprehension beta/eta laws;
* the represented syntactic natural model of generalized elements, with
  intrinsically indexed variables and substitution-stable dependent products,
  dependent sums, and identity types; introduction and elimination construct
  judgments directly, while beta remains proof-relevant formed-endpoint
  conversion rather than host-language equality, including explicit type
  transport for the dependent second projection; a displayed-universe
  refinement makes every conversion intermediate intrinsically typed and
  proves that forgetting this evidence commutes with typed substitution;
  the declaration-aware
  fixed-left identity eliminator and its authored iota witness embed as a
  substitution-stable native cell in the same judgmental natural model;
* a scoped Russell/generated-Tarski presentation boundary, extended by typed
  contextual templates for open families, with the generated grammar proved
  to be exactly the zero-template fragment;
* proof-relevant judgment-indexed computation and conversion evidence, with
  raw declaration equations admitted only through explicit preservation;
  authored/native receipt comparison is separately required to be natural in
  renaming and simultaneous substitution before it transports complete typed
  occurrences, a capability proved for List/identity and both candidate views
  of the shared Nat/Vec declaration world without postulating a universal
  conversion checker; the authored and native receipt relations are mutually
  inverse equipment cells, and their renaming/substitution naturality laws are
  equalities of composed proof-relevant cells;
* generic open algebraic schemas, parallel reduction, and occurrence-separated
  presentations whose fibre evidence may retain proof-relevant conversion
  receipts; exact nonlinear tower iota schemas are related conservatively to
  their left-linear occurrence geometry, while the remaining Church--Rosser
  choice is exposed by a machine-checked negative control rather than assumed;
* explicit polymorphic functional composition and Church-list map derivations;
* a generic layered native proof-family extension for arbitrary declared HOL
  interfaces, preserving source computation through the existing extension
  morphism and instantiated independently by the List and call-guard theories;
  open judgments attach along arbitrary presentation morphisms and typed
